  "body": "## Description\r\nFixes an error when using torch compiled code inside a checkpointed region.\r\n\r\nthe error was reported [here](https://github.com/ecmwf/anemoi-core/issues/1330) with more background [here](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/166926). The fix comes from [here](https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/1991) and is only available for torch 2.10 and above. I have added a warning if you use compilation and torch < 2.10 which lists some workarounds. but the proper solution is upgrading torch.\r\n\r\nIt also fixes another cause of recompilation errors: `torch._inductor.config.shape_padding` can pad tensors based on micro-benchmarks. if you recompile inside a checkpointed reason this can lead to shape mismatches. I disable this feature when using gradient checkpointing. I also warn users about other settings e.g. \"mode='max-autotune'\" which could lead to errors when used with gradient checkpointing. \r\n\r\nLastly, I set a default number of CPU threads. Otherwise this was being reset multiple times by PytorchLightning during runtime. Each time it was set, it would trigger a needless recompilation, which used up one of the 'model.recompile_limit' recompilations\r\n\r\nI got Claude to generate a reproducer, using the compiled conditional layer norm in anemoi (see [here](https://github.com/ecmwf/anemoi-core/blob/3cb72df1f1767b8588b518b0c6e9af98f3e4893c/reproduce_compile_checkpoint_lru.py)) the error fires when the cache is enabled, and doesn't fire when the cache is disabled.\r\n\r\nBy opening this pull request, I affirm that all authors agree to the [Contributor License Agreement.](https://github.com/ecmwf/codex/blob/main/Legal/Contributor-License-Agreement.md)\r\n",
